commit cb0d28afdfe39cffdfa43f2e3a2160a194f21d96
Author: Maykel Moya <mmoya@mmoya.org>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 15:04:45 2026 +0200

    Complete TX NAPI on early exit to avoid napi_disable() hang
    
    ax_tx_poll_qx() bails out with "return -1" when the device is unplugged,
    disabled, or has no carrier, without calling napi_complete_done(). The
    NAPI core treats any return value below the budget as "done" and drops
    the instance from the poll list, but only the driver can clear
    NAPI_STATE_SCHED. The instance therefore stays scheduled forever, and
    the next napi_disable() on it loops in usleep_range() indefinitely.
    
    The race is easy to hit: ax_start_xmit() schedules tx_napi without
    looking at the carrier, so a frame queued just before the link drops
    (e.g. on resume from suspend) leads to a poll that sees
    !netif_carrier_ok() and takes the early exit.
    
    Observed on 6.18.55-1-lts with an AX88179A (0b95:1790) after resume:
    the carrier dropped, NetworkManager took the interface down, and
    ax_close() blocked in napi_disable(&tx_napi[i]) while holding RTNL:
    
      napi_disable_locked+0xf0/0x100
      napi_disable+0x25/0x40
      ax_close+0x63/0x160 [ax_usb_nic]
      __dev_close_many
      __dev_change_flags
      netif_change_flags
      do_setlink.isra.0
      rtnl_newlink
    
    Every other RTNL user (geoclue, avahi, browsers, systemd-resolved
    clients) then hung in rtnl_dumpit() in D state. The link-down branch
    of ax_set_carrier() also calls napi_disable(&tx_napi[i]) and is
    exposed to the same hang from a kworker.
    
    Complete NAPI on every early-exit path and return 0; a poll function
    must never return a negative value. No work is lost: TX is rescheduled
    by ax_set_carrier() / __ax_work_func() once the carrier comes back.
    The RX poll path already completes correctly, and the tasklet build
    (ENABLE_TX_TASKLET) is unaffected.
    
    Guarding in ax_close() instead is not viable: napi_disable() has no
    timeout variant, and skipping it would let the poll function run
    against buffers that ax_free_buffer() is about to free.

diff --git a/src/ax_main.c b/src/ax_main.c
index 5f1cddb..c722bce 100644
--- a/src/ax_main.c
+++ b/src/ax_main.c
@@ -1497,8 +1497,10 @@ static int ax_tx_poll_qx(struct ax_device *axdev, struct napi_struct *tx_napi,
 
 	if (test_bit(AX_UNPLUG, &axdev->flags) ||
 	    !test_bit(AX_ENABLE, &axdev->flags) ||
-	    !netif_carrier_ok(axdev->netdev))
-		return -1;
+	    !netif_carrier_ok(axdev->netdev)) {
+		napi_complete_done(tx_napi, 0);
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	clear_bit(AX_SCHEDULE_NAPI_TX, &axdev->flags);
 
